  "privInShortTitle": "In short",
  "privInShort": "Playground Tracker does not collect personal data. There is no account, no server of ours, no analytics, no advertising and no tracking. The developer cannot see your log.",
  "privStoresTitle": "What the app stores",
  "privStores": "The names of the parents and kids you enter, your visits (date, morning or evening, who went, which kids, how long, activities, and any reason you give), your plans and how they went, and your settings. All of it is kept in the app’s private storage on your iPhone.",
  "privICloudTitle": "iCloud sync and family sharing",
  "privICloud": "If you are signed in to iCloud, the app keeps a copy in your own private iCloud database through Apple’s CloudKit, so it stays in sync across your devices. If you invite family members with a share link, the people you invite can see and edit the shared log until you stop sharing. iCloud data is handled by Apple under Apple’s privacy policy; the developer has no access to it.",
  "privRemindersTitle": "Reminders",
  "privReminders": "Reminder notifications are scheduled on your iPhone. Nothing about them is sent anywhere. The app asks for permission only when you turn a reminder on.",
  "privCalendarTitle": "Calendar and Reminders",
  "privCalendar": "Add to Calendar opens Apple’s own event editor with the plan filled in. The app does not read your calendar; the event is saved only if you tap Add. Add to Reminders saves the plan as one new reminder in your Reminders app. The app does not read your reminders and nothing is sent anywhere.",
  "privChildrenTitle": "Children",
  "privChildren": "The app is meant for parents. Children’s names stay on your iPhone and in your own iCloud. Nothing about children is sent to the developer or to anyone else.",
  "privDeletingTitle": "Deleting your data",
  "privDeleting": "Settings › Delete all data removes everything at once, from your iPhone and from your iCloud; if you share the log with family, it is removed for them too. You can also delete single entries at any time, and deleting the app removes everything stored on the iPhone. To stop sharing, use Family sync in Settings.",
